---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import SectionPhoto from '../../components/SectionPhoto.astro';
import { localePath } from '../../lib/i18n';

const locale = 'en' as const;
---

<BaseLayout
  locale={locale}
  title="About — Yardage"
  description="Yardage makes the yardage book accessible to clubs and players of every level."
>
  <Header locale={locale} />
  <main>
    <Hero
      locale={locale}
      title="About"
      subtitle="Our ambition is to make the yardage book accessible to clubs and players of every level."
      image="/images/bg-fairway.jpg"
      compact
    />

    <SectionPhoto image="/images/bg-trees.jpg">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink md:text-3xl">An idea born on the course</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Yardage was not born in an office. It was born on the course.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Victor discovered golf at seven. Over the years, it became a true discipline: a permanent
          learning curve built on precision, strategy and high standards.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          In early 2019, he passed that passion on to Rodolphe, his cousin. Shared rounds gradually gave
          way to a deeper involvement, including competing together at a high amateur level.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          In 2021, Rodolphe caddied for Victor at a national amateur championship. That experience was a
          turning point. Preparing the course and watching what players needed, we saw a clear gap:
          professional yardage books remained hard for amateurs to access.
        </p>
      </SectionPhoto>

    <SectionPhoto image="/images/bg-aerial.jpg">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink md:text-3xl">The observation behind Yardage</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          In high-level golf, the yardage book is a real working tool. It helps understand the shape of
          a hole, identify hazards, visualise distances and prepare a suitable strategy.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Outside the professional circuit, however, its use remains very limited.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Our observation is simple:</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          <li>the yardage book offer is underdeveloped in France;</li>
          <li>professional materials are rarely accessible to amateur players;</li>
          <li>quality and content vary widely from one club to another;</li>
          <li>
            there is no shared standard that lets players find a clear, familiar reading on every
            course;
          </li>
          <li>
            many clubs have no support truly adapted to their course and their identity.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          The problem was therefore not only the occasional absence of a book. It was a broader lack of
          structure and consistency.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          From one club to another, a player might find a detailed booklet, a summary sheet or, most
          often, nothing at all. We decided that gap needed filling — for clubs and for their players’
          experience.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          The idea of Yardage was born from that factual observation.
        </p>
      </SectionPhoto>

    <SectionPhoto image="/images/bg-green.jpg">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink md:text-3xl">From observation to first prototype</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Ten months after our first observation, we presented our first book at the 2022 Grand Prix of
          Golf d’Ableiges.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          That first operation was the real launch of the project.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          The prototype was still relatively simple and did not yet include elevation. Data came from
          satellite imagery, then was completed and verified on the ground.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          This first version let us test the idea against the reality of the course. We could watch how
          players used the book, identify truly useful information and measure what needed improving
          through feedback.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          The Ableiges prototype was not yet the final product. It was proof that our project met a
          concrete need.
        </p>
      </SectionPhoto>

    <SectionPhoto image="/images/bg-fairway.jpg">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink md:text-3xl">Four years of development</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          After that first operation, we began a long process of development, structure and
          industrialisation.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          For four years, we refined our method to move from a prototype built for one competition to a
          solution that can be deployed consistently across different courses.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Each step helped us improve:</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          <li>data collection and processing;</li>
          <li>accuracy of representations;</li>
          <li>overall readability of the books;</li>
          <li>graphic consistency across courses;</li>
          <li>integration of each club’s own identity;</li>
          <li>reproducibility of the production process;</li>
          <li>print quality and product durability;</li>
          <li>lead times and manufacturing costs.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Early surveys combined satellite data with on-course observation. Our process now relies
          mainly on satellite data, through a method gradually refined and standardised.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          That evolution lets us produce more efficiently while keeping a constant standard of care.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          After four years of development, Yardage is entering a new phase with its final version —
          the result of all research, trials and improvements since the first prototype.
        </p>
      </SectionPhoto>

    <SectionPhoto image="/images/bg-trees.jpg">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink md:text-3xl">
          A shared standard, an identity unique to each club
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          We do not want to produce one-off books whose structure and quality change from project to
          project.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">We want to establish a true standard.</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Every Yardage book should offer a clear, consistent, immediately understandable reading. A
          player discovering a new course should find the same landmarks and the same logic of use.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          That consistency does not mean every book must look the same.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Every club has its history, architecture, particularities and identity. Our work is to
          reconcile two requirements:
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Build a shared professional structure while respecting the singularity of each course.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          The product must be identifiable as a Yardage book — and as the official book of the club it
          was designed for.
        </p>
      </SectionPhoto>

    <SectionPhoto image="/images/bg-aerial.jpg">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink md:text-3xl">A company built by two</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Yardage is a family project that we build together.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          We both work across the business: design, product development, commercial strategy, club
          relationships, production and brand evolution.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          That shared involvement lets us keep a coherent vision from the first contact with a club
          through to book delivery.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Victor has worked in hospitality since 2012. That path gave him a strong culture of service,
          operational standards and customer satisfaction. In that world, quality is not only the
          product — it is also consistency, presentation and the overall experience offered.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          The same logic guides Yardage: offer clubs a professional, reliable solution that is simple
          to integrate into how they operate.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Our complementary skills bring together golf knowledge, course experience, commercial
          development and a constant search for a more effective solution.
        </p>
      </SectionPhoto>

    <SectionPhoto image="/images/bg-green.jpg">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink md:text-3xl">Our promise to clubs</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          A golf course is sporting, landscape and architectural heritage. It deserves a support that
          presents it accurately and values the work done by the club.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Our promise is clear:</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Give every club the means to offer a professional, consistent yardage book in its own image.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">For clubs, Yardage should become:</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          <li>a tool to showcase the course;</li>
          <li>an extra service for members and visitors;</li>
          <li>a support aligned with their standards;</li>
          <li>a way to strengthen their image;</li>
          <li>
            a concrete answer to players’ needs in competition and casual rounds alike.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Our goal is to make creating a professional book simpler and more accessible, without
          imposing complex technical work on the club.
        </p>
      </SectionPhoto>

    <SectionPhoto image="/images/bg-fairway.jpg">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink md:text-3xl">Our promise to players</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          We want to make course information long associated with professional golf accessible to
          amateurs.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          The book does not replace experience, judgement or execution. It does help the player
          understand what lies ahead and make decisions with better information.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Our promise to players is therefore:</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Make the course information used at the highest level accessible to everyone.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">A Yardage book should help you:</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          <li>visualise each hole more clearly;</li>
          <li>anticipate the main difficulties;</li>
          <li>prepare a strategy before the round;</li>
          <li>choose a line of play more clearly;</li>
          <li>better understand distances and key areas;</li>
          <li>approach the course with more confidence.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Our ambition is not to tell the player how to play, but to give them what they need to build
          their own strategy.
        </p>
      </SectionPhoto>

    <SectionPhoto image="/images/bg-trees.jpg">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink md:text-3xl">
          A French ambition, open to the world
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Yardage is growing today with French golf clubs.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Our method and product are also designed to adapt to other countries. We remain open to
          projects and proposals from clubs abroad.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          In the long run, our goal is to make the yardage book a natural part of what a club offers —
          not a rare tool reserved for certain events or a minority of players.
        </p>
      </SectionPhoto>

    <SectionPhoto image="/images/bg-aerial.jpg">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink md:text-3xl">Our vision</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Yardage rests on a simple belief:</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Every course deserves a book equal to its identity. Every player deserves to understand it.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          We want to build a brand that is both technical and premium, founded on precision,
          consistency and quality.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          A brand able to establish a shared standard without erasing the personality of clubs.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          A brand born from experience on the ground and developed to meet a real need.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          From the first observation to the first prototype, then through four years of development, our
          goal has stayed the same: make the professional yardage book more accessible, more consistent
          and more useful.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">For clubs and for players.</p>

        <p class="mt-12 font-display text-xl text-ink">Victor &amp; Rodolphe</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-soft">Co-founders of Yardage</p>

        <div class="mt-10">
          <a
            href={localePath(locale, 'contact')}
            class="inline-flex rounded-sm bg-brand px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-ink"
          >
            Talk about your course
          </a>
        </div>
      </SectionPhoto>
  </main>
  <Footer locale={locale} />
</BaseLayout>
